# Admin auth: never create a redirect loop

Login stores the same admin JWT in two places:
- the httpOnly cookie `glimps_admin_session` (shared by all tabs, read on the server);
- `sessionStorage['glimps_admin_token']` (per tab, sent as `Authorization: Bearer` to `/api/*`).

A loop happens when one page redirects on one copy and the other page on the other copy
(2026-10-03: a new tab had the cookie but no token, and `/login` and `/dashboard` bounced forever).

## Rules

1. **The cookie decides.** Only `src/app/login/layout.tsx` (server) may redirect `/login` → `/dashboard`.
   Never redirect away from `/login` based on sessionStorage.
2. **The dashboard layout syncs the token.** After `getMyProfileAction()` passes, it always copies
   the cookie's JWT into sessionStorage (`getAdminTokenFromSessionAction` + `setAdminJwtInSessionStorage`)
   before rendering pages. Pages may rely on the token being present.
3. **Leaving for /login always clears both copies.** Use `signOutToLogin(router)` from
   `src/lib/admin-sign-out.ts` — never a bare `router.replace('/login')` or `window.location.href = '/login'`.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — the cookie survives, /login sends the user straight back
.catch(() => router.replace('/login'));

// ✅ GOOD
.catch(() => void signOutToLogin(router));
```

4. Log out must not depend on a Bearer-protected API to clear the cookie (`signOutToLogin` uses a server action).
5. The cookie's `maxAge` must match the JWT TTL (`getAdminJwtTtlSeconds()`), so both expire together.
6. Any new protected admin page goes under `src/app/dashboard/` (it inherits the layout's check and token sync).

## Before deploying

`ADMIN_JWT_SECRET` set (long, random, same on every instance); the proxy forwards `X-Forwarded-Proto`.
After deploying: log in, open a new tab, log out, log in, delete the cookie and reload — never a loop.
